# SAME70Q20B USB-CDC boot/connect smoke test. Exercises the
# CONFIG_ATSAM_USB firmware variant (duet3-6hc / duet3-6xd printer
# configs are USB+CAN-only on real hardware, no serial-mode firmware
# variant exists) against the local USBHS Renode peripheral
# (test/emulator/repl/same70_usbhs.cs). The peripheral uses a
# "skip-enum cheat" - inject a SET_CONFIGURATION SETUP packet on EP0
# so klipper's CDC stack reaches bulk-active without a full USB host
# emulation - then exposes BULK_IN/BULK_OUT as a UART pipe to the
# host pty via UARTBase. The companion same70_smoke.test covers the
# CONFIG_ATSAM_SERIAL path; both share the same .repl (USBHS is
# resident unconditionally and stays idle when the firmware never
# touches it).
#
# KNOWN BLOCKED (the one remaining EMULATOR test that does not pass
# under --force-emulator). Diagnosis below is from clean-host runs on a
# native-Linux x86_64 box (deterministic, not the disk-pressured macOS
# Docker that masked these as flaky):
# Root cause is a two-sided SysTick-vs-DWT timing tension in the SAME70
# model - it is NOT about Renode free-run vs deterministic execution
# (confirmed: it fails identically in tick mode, which does not free-run):
#   * SysTick=450MHz (upstream platforms/cpus/sam_e70.repl) vs DWT=300MHz
#     (the 300MHz core clock / CONFIG_CLOCK_FREQ that klipper's SysTick
#     CLKSOURCE=processor and DWT->CYCCNT both use): the skip-enum cheat
#     works end-to-end - enumeration completes, klippy reaches "Loaded MCU
#     'mcu'" with ~110 BULK_IN transfers - but the SysTick fires ~1.5x
#     early, so klipper's timer_dispatch_many busy-waits for a far deadline
#     while OTHER scheduled timers fall >1ms behind DWT, tripping
#     static_string_id 56 "Rescheduled timer in the past" (armcm_timer.c).
#     klippy then sees is_shutdown at config-send.
#   * SysTick=300MHz (matching DWT/CLOCK_FREQ - the "correct" value):
#     removes the reason-56 shutdown, but the firmware's USB EORST handler
#     then never enables RXSTPES on EP0, so the skip-enum SETUP never
#     injects and identify never starts. (A USBHS-model / firmware-USB
#     timing dependency on the SysTick rate.)
#   * Tried + ruled out: cpu MaximumBlockSize sweep 1..1024
#     (RENODE_EXP_BLOCKSIZE), small SetGlobalQuantum (RENODE_EXP_QUANTUM),
#     RENODE_EXP_MIPS (hides reason-56 but breaks enumeration), and tick
#     mode with both SysTick rates - none satisfy both sides.
#   * Remaining fix shape: make the USBHS EORST/SETUP bringup work at the
#     correct 300MHz SysTick (so reason-56 stays gone AND enumeration
#     completes). This is the one EMULATOR test still blocked; everything
#     else passes under --force-emulator on a clean host.
DICTIONARY same70q20b-usb.dict
CONFIG same70_usb_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR same70_usb_smoke.fixture.json

# A few harmless gcode lines so klippy gets past klippy:ready.
M114
M105
M105
M105

# klippy connected and stayed connected long enough to do the
# clocksync handshake against the firmware's generic/armcm_timer view
# transported over the synthetic USBHS bulk endpoints.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
